index 0000000..5ecce98
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SOLUTION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Solution
+
+Two bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`, both in the LRU bookkeeping:
+
+1. **`get` did not refresh recency.** On a cache hit it returned the value
+   without calling `move_to_end`, so reads never counted as "use" and a
+   recently read key could still be evicted as the least-recently-used entry.
+   Fixed by moving the key to the MRU end on every successful `get`.
+
+2. **`put` evicted on in-place updates.** The eviction check only looked at
+   `len(self._data) >= self.capacity`, so overwriting an existing key at
+   capacity still popped the LRU entry even though the size wasn't growing.
+   Fixed by evicting only when the key is not already present.
